# Redux Store

Store uses Redux Toolkit with a **dynamic slice factory** (`getSlice`) instead of a per-feature slice pattern. All reducers are auto-generated from `EnumStoreKeys` — no manual registration required.

## Folder layout — `src/stores/`

```
src/stores/
  root-stores.ts          // configureStore + auto-builds reducers from EnumStoreKeys
  redux-slide.tsx         // getSlice(key, initialState) factory — DO NOT touch when adding a new store
  stores.constants.ts     // EnumStoreKeys + storesInitialState (entry point for new stores)
  models/
    stores-<feature>.model.ts   // EnumStores<Feature>Properties + Stores<Feature>Model
  index.ts                // re-exports root-stores only
```

> Note: the file should be named `redux-slice.tsx` but it is currently `redux-slide.tsx` (typo). Keep it as-is — many places already import from this path.

## Adding a new store (3 steps, NO per-feature slice/middleware)

### 1. Create the model — `src/stores/models/stores-<feature>.model.ts`

- Declare `EnumStores<Feature>Properties` for all property keys (string enum).
- Declare interface `Stores<Feature>Model` using `[EnumStores<Feature>Properties.X]` as keys.

```ts
// src/stores/models/stores-user-info.model.ts
export enum EnumStoresUserInfoProperties {
  ID = "id",
  TITLE = "title",
}

export interface StoresUserInfoModel {
  [EnumStoresUserInfoProperties.ID]: number;
  [EnumStoresUserInfoProperties.TITLE]: string;
}
```

### 2. Register the key + initial state — `src/stores/stores.constants.ts`

- Add a new member to `EnumStoreKeys`.
- Add the matching initial state to `storesInitialState`, using the property enum as keys (never hardcode raw strings).

```ts
export enum EnumStoreKeys {
  USER_INFO = "user_info",
  // FOO_BAR = "foo_bar",   // add here
}

export const storesInitialState: Record<EnumStoreKeys, any> = {
  [EnumStoreKeys.USER_INFO]: {
    [EnumStoresUserInfoProperties.ID]: 1,
    [EnumStoresUserInfoProperties.TITLE]: "okoko",
  },
};
```

### 3. Done

You do NOT need to edit `root-stores.ts`: `getAllReducers()` iterates `Object.values(EnumStoreKeys)` and calls `getSlice(key, storesInitialState[key])` to produce a reducer keyed by the same store name.

## Consuming a store — the `useGetReduxStores` hook

Do NOT import raw `useSelector` / `useDispatch`, and do NOT touch slices directly. Always go through `useGetReduxStores`:

```tsx
import { useGetReduxStores } from "@src/hooks/use-get-redux-stores";
import { EnumStoreKeys } from "@src/stores/stores.constants";
import { EnumStoresUserInfoProperties } from "@src/stores/models/stores-user-info.model";

const userInfoStore = useGetReduxStores(EnumStoreKeys.USER_INFO);

// Read — always use the property enum, never hardcode "id" / "title"
const id = userInfoStore?.getData(EnumStoresUserInfoProperties.ID);
const title = userInfoStore?.getData(EnumStoresUserInfoProperties.TITLE);

// Write — payload is a partial object shaped like Stores<Feature>Model
userInfoStore?.setData({
  [EnumStoresUserInfoProperties.ID]: 9,
  [EnumStoresUserInfoProperties.TITLE]: "ok9",
});
```

- `getData(key)` supports dot-notation paths (e.g. `"profile.address.city"`) and returns `undefined` if any segment is missing.
- `setData(payload)` is implemented by the `setData` reducer in `redux-slide.tsx`: it iterates `Object.keys(state)` and assigns `state[key] = action.payload[key]`. This means **any key missing in the payload becomes `undefined`**. Always pass the full property set, or merge with current state before dispatching.

## Required conventions

- Store key: `EnumStoreKeys.<UPPER_SNAKE> = "<lower_snake>"` (e.g. `USER_INFO = "user_info"`).
- Model file: `stores-<feature>.model.ts` inside `src/stores/models/`.
- Property enum: `EnumStores<PascalFeature>Properties` (string enum, lowercase values).
- State interface: `Stores<PascalFeature>Model`.
- NEVER hardcode property strings — always use `EnumStores<Feature>Properties.X`.
- DO NOT create per-feature `redux-slice.ts` / `middleware.ts` / `data-type.ts` files in the old pattern — that pattern has been replaced.
- `src/stores/index.ts` is a barrel only: `export * from "./root-stores"`. No logic.

## Typed selector / dispatch (when needed)

`root-stores.ts` still exports:

- `store`, `RootState`, `AppDispatch`
- `useAppDispatch`, `useAppSelector` (typed wrappers around `react-redux`)
- `allReducerMapData` — a `EnumStoreKeys → { setData, reducer }` map (used internally by `useGetReduxStores`; do not call from components).

Components should normally only need `useGetReduxStores`. Fall back to `useAppSelector` / `useAppDispatch` only for special cases not covered by `getData` / `setData` (e.g. selecting from multiple stores at once with custom memoization).

## Thunks / side-effects

The per-feature `middleware.ts` thunk pattern from the old rule is gone. Place side-effects (API calls) in:

- `@tanstack/react-query` for fetching/caching (preferred).
- Or plain functions calling `src/requests/api/...`, then sync the result into the store via `setData(...)` from a component/hook.

Never call `axios` directly — always go through `src/requests/api/<domain>`.
